                <note rend="inline" type="source">722.2315/2489: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-31T16:00:00-05:00">October 31, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>584. My telegram No. 579, October 30, noon. The Argentine Ambassador was told by
                    the Ecuadoran Minister to Peru that the presence at Lima of the Peruvian
                    Minister to Ecuador is not related to direct boundary negotiations since no such
                    negotiations are in progress. The Ecuadoran Minister expressed the opinion that
                    the 1936 line would be most satisfactory to Ecuador as a basis for discussions
                    but that if concessions were made to Peru at some points Ecuador would want
                    compensation without <hi rendition="#italic">putuma traduce</hi> [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">sic</hi>]. He will report confidentially to his
                    Government regarding his conversation with the Argentine Ambassador and inform
                    the latter of any Ecuadoran views received in reply.</p>
                <p>Unless the Department insists on [<hi rendition="#italic">or?</hi>] the Foreign
                    Offices of Argentina and Brazil instruct to the contrary my colleague[s] and I
                    will continue our conversations with the Peruvian Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    and our informal soundings with the Ecuadoran Minister.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
